SimpleDoc -- simpler documentation for functions and methods
************************************************************

Description
===========

This package provides a simple, human-readable text format for documentation
nodes as an alternative to the classic *note hypertext list format:
(Macaulay2Doc)hypertext list format, accepted by the *note document(List):
(Macaulay2Doc)document, function.

The new format is accepted by the *note doc(String): doc, function for writing
either a single or multiple documentation nodes from a string or file and
adheres to the off-side rule (see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/off-side_rule
), i.e., using indentation to separate blocks.



Getting started with SimpleDoc

  * *note Writing documentation in Macaulay2: (Macaulay2Doc)writing
    documentation,
  * *note Using SimpleDoc for documentation: doc,
  * *note Using markup in documentation: (Text)Top,
  * *note Using TeX in documentation: (Text)html_lpTEX_rp,

Templates for using the *note doc(String): doc, method

  * *note docExample: docExample, -- an example of a documentation string
  * *note docTemplate: doc, -- a simple documentation function
  * *note packageTemplate: packageTemplate, -- a template for a package

Documentation helpers

  * *note arXiv: arXiv, -- link to an arXiv article
  * *note stacksProject: stacksProject, -- link to a Stacks Project tag
  * *note wikipedia: wikipedia, -- link to a Wikipedia article

