testExample -- an example of a test string
******************************************

  * Usage: 
        testExample

Description
===========

The variable testExample is a *note String: (Macaulay2Doc)String, containing an
example of the use of *note TEST: (Macaulay2Doc)TEST, to write a test case.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|TEST /// -* test for simpleDocFrob *-                                  |
|  assert(simpleDocFrob(2,matrix{{1,2}}) == matrix{{1,2,0,0},{0,0,1,2}})|
|///                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

The *note check: (Macaulay2Doc)check, method executes all package tests defined
this way.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : check SimpleDoc                                             |
| -- capturing check(0, "SimpleDoc")           -- .240572s elapsed|
| -- capturing check(1, "SimpleDoc")           -- .286169s elapsed|
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note TEST: (Macaulay2Doc)TEST, -- add a test for a package
  * *note check: (Macaulay2Doc)check, -- perform tests of a package
  * *note packageTemplate: packageTemplate, -- a template for a package
  * *note docExample: docExample, -- an example of a documentation string

For the programmer
==================

